## First-time setup

```bash
uv sync
```
{% if include_database %}

```bash
cp .env.example .env   # fill in DATABASE_URL if it differs from the default
uv run alembic upgrade head
```
{% elif include_ai_service or include_auth or include_observability %}

```bash
cp .env.example .env   # fill in the secrets below
```
{% endif %}
{% if include_ai_service %}

Fill in `.env`'s LLM credentials matching `ai.llm.provider` in `config.yaml` (default: `{{ llm_provider_default }}`).
{% endif %}
{% if include_auth %}

Generate an API key: `python scripts/manage_api_keys.py create --label "local-dev"` (prints the raw key once — save it).
{% endif %}

**Commit `uv.lock` on your first commit** — CI's `uv sync --frozen` depends on it existing.

## Running it
{% if include_backend or include_worker or include_database or include_cache %}

**With Docker:**
```bash
docker compose up -d --build
```
(`docker-compose.override.yml` is merged automatically — hot reload is on by default.)
{% endif %}
{% if include_backend or include_worker or include_docs_site %}

**Natively** (requires{% if include_database %} Postgres{% endif %}{% if include_worker %} and RabbitMQ{% endif %} already running):
```bash
process-compose up
```
Or run pieces individually:
{% if include_backend %}
```bash
uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```
{% endif %}
{% if include_worker %}
```bash
uv run python -m app.worker.main
```
{% endif %}
{% if include_docs_site %}
```bash
uv run mkdocs serve -a 0.0.0.0:8001
```
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if include_observability %}

**Metrics dashboards** (optional, on top of the above):
```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.observability.yml up -d
```
Grafana at `http://localhost:${GRAFANA_PORT:-3001}` (default login `admin`/`admin`, set `GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD` in `.env` to change it).
{% endif %}

